Task: Backend-Served SPA Deep-Link Validation

Summary: Implemented static file serving with SPA deep-link fallback for the Fastify backend server.

Changes:
- Created server/src/api/staticServing.ts with registerStaticServing function
- Created server/src/api/staticServing.test.ts with 17 integration tests
- Updated server/src/main.ts to register static serving from app/dist

Key behaviors:
- Serves static assets (JS, CSS, images, fonts) with correct MIME types
- Falls back to index.html for SPA routes (dashboard, library/*, settings/*, etc.)
- Does NOT serve index.html for /api/* routes (passes through to API handlers)
- Does NOT serve index.html for missing static files (returns 404)
- Handles missing static directory gracefully

Files created/modified:
- server/src/api/staticServing.ts (new)
- server/src/api/staticServing.test.ts (new)
- server/src/main.ts (modified)

Why: Required for production deployment where the Bun backend serves the Vite-built React SPA directly, enabling deep-linking to client-side routes.
